      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2012 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "A structure-activity relationship study was undertaken to address the lack of oral exposure of the H3 antagonist 1, which incorporated an arylketone. Among a number of sub-series, the 4H-pyrido[1,2-a]pyrimidin-4-one analog 21 showed an improved PK profile in rat and mouse and was active in an obesity model. The pyrimidin-4-one proved to be a novel and useful ketone bioisostere."
      },
